#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# down_values

#% text
# `down_values(f)` gives the rules defined for calls `f(...)`, as `lhs :> rhs` with the left side as it was written, in the order they are tried (the most specific first). `down_values("f")` takes the name as a string.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A definition with optional arguments is listed once, as written. Built-in code and the catch-all a `fn` adds for arguments that match no clause are not listed.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
rule fact(0) := 1

#% cell
rule fact(k_) := k * fact(k - 1)

#% cell
down_values(fact)
#% output
#= [fact(0) :> 1, fact(k_) :> k*fact(k - 1)]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The listed rules can be applied by hand:

#% cell
rewrite(quote(fact(3)), down_values(fact))
#% output
#= quote(3*fact(3 - 1))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `up_values`, `sub_values`, `own_values`, `names`
